WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.169
-Now, you guys
are obviously super close.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.205
I have been around both of you,
and it's just --

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.906
You work so well off each other.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.342
But I want to see how close
you guys actually are.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:13.345
With that in mind, it is time
for the Father-Son Challenge.

00:00:13.345 --> 00:00:15.748
-♪ "Tonight Show" ♪

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:18.218
♪ Father-Son Challenge ♪

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.218
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:20.686
-Yeah, so here's how it works.

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.122
One of you will --
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.457
-One of you will mute your audio
while the other one answers...

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:27.860
-He's so happy!
-...a question about you.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.097
And then you'll unmute, and
we'll see if they were correct.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.299
If your answer matches,
you get a point.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.002
You ready for this?
-Yes.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:39.638
-All right, Lin,
can you please mute your audio?

00:00:39.638 --> 00:00:44.077
-Yes, sir.
One sec.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.112
-All right.
Luis, here's the question.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.114
Okay?
-Yes.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:52.819
-What was Lin's dream job
when he was a kid?

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.622
-He wanted to be a filmmaker.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:59.225
And he always walked around
with a camera

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.327
and filmed figurines

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:05.497
and filmed anything
he could get his hands on.

00:01:05.497 --> 00:01:06.632
-I was gonna say that.

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:09.001
I would say that
or a rock star or something.

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:10.236
-[ Laughs ]
-But, yes, all right.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.236
That's good.
Okay, good.

00:01:11.236 --> 00:01:13.273
That's really -- okay.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:18.978
All right, Lin, you hit unmute.
Good.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.947
That was my signal for unmute.
It was a lot of hand-flapping.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.315
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.684
-Flapping hands.
You're a star!

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.486
-I could be your adopted son
if you want to.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.288
[ Laughter ]
All right.

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:31.424
Lin, the question was,

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:35.094
what was your dream job
when you were a kid?

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.729
-Oh, I wanted to make movies.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.231
I wanted to be Steven Spielberg
when I was a kid.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.433
[ Ding! ]
Hey!

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.701
-[ Laughs ]
-Everyone knows that.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.903
-That is fantastic.
That's so good.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.738
Okay.
Luis, you're up.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.974
Please mute your audio.

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:51.177
-[ Laughs ]
-All right. Now he's muted.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.378
All right, good.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.712
-Good, he's muted.
Okay, good.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.448
He can't hear us, but we can
still hear him weirdly.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.383
His mic is on.
Okay. So, here we go.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.584
Ready?

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:03.356
Lin, what is your dad's
go-to karaoke song?

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.291
-Oh.
Um...

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.360
It's either --
Can I give you two?

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.628
-Yep.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.763
-It's either, "I've Had
the Time of My Life"...

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.199
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:18.037
-He played that song
in our Subaru a solid year.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.705
And I just wanted to hear
"Be My Baby,"

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.908
which was the next track on
the "Dirty Dancing" soundtrack.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.845
He would just hit rewind,
play it again.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:30.750
That or, it's probably, like,
"Greatest Showman."

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.486
[ Laughs ] It's probably
"This is the Greatest Show."

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:34.487
-Really?
-He's like a --

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.189
He's a "Greatest Showman's" fan.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:37.924
He's got a red jacket
and everything.

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.525
-No way.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.326
-I love that.
I was gonna say --

00:02:41.326 --> 00:02:44.163
I was gonna say
"Sound of Music."

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.466
-Oh, yeah.
That's entirely possible, too.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.600
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.002
-I never had a chance
at another living.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.837
It was always
gonna be show tunes.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:56.509
[ Laughs ]
-All right. Luis?

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.145
All right, the question was --

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:02.215
I asked Lin, "What is your dad's
go-to karaoke song?"

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:04.951
-Well, it depends where in life.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:08.821
You know, for a long time now,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.856
it has been
"The Greatest Showman."

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:14.593
-[ Laughs ]
[ Ding! ]

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:15.661
-That's what he said.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:17.730
He said,
it's "Greatest Showman."

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.232
You're a big
"Greatest Showman" fan.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.633
I love that.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.234
Hugh Jackman.
I love that you love that.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.971
-I was gonna wear
my red jacket today.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.906
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my gosh.
[ Ding! ]

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.307
That's a double.
You get double points.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:30.176
-Do I get an extra point
for that?

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.211
I told him, "He's got the red
jacket and everything."

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:35.081
-[ Laughs ]
-That's good.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.483
He said the other one
could've been

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:40.720
"I've Had the Time of My Life."
-From "Dirty Dancing."

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.989
-♪ Time of my life ♪
Yes.

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:46.392
[ Laughter ]
-He said that played a lot.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:51.230
-My wife always wanted to do the
jumping, and I would catch her.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.198
-Yeah, I mean --
-Never happened.

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:54.400
-Never happened.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.636
-Hey, you know.
You gotta have goals, right?

00:03:57.636 --> 00:03:58.871
Okay.
Here we go.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.072
Final round.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.208
Lin, please mute yourself.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.046
Wow.
He just took the headphones off.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.347
There we go.
All right.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:10.082
Luis, here's the question.

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:14.988
What is Lin's most embarrassing
childhood memory?

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:18.891
-He got summons
and sort of arrested

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:22.361
for singing in the subway
with friends,

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:26.832
collecting money,
while he was going to school.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:30.002
-Wow.
I mean, yeah, it's trouble,

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.537
but I feel like he would
probably think that's cool.

00:04:32.537 --> 00:04:33.772
But I will take that.

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:35.407
-That is not cool at all!

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:36.743
-No, it's not cool.
Do not get arrested.

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:37.943
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:40.312
But I feel like a little doo-wop
is kind of fun.

00:04:40.312 --> 00:04:42.615
[ Laughs ]

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.984
-Not when the cops stop you.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.118
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
You're right.

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:47.753
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's true, yeah.

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:48.955
All right. Not cool.
Here we go.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.990
Not cool.
Lin?

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.261
All right.
All right, here we go.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.462
Can you hear us?

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.965
-I'm terrified
by the gesticulation I saw.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.032
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:03.235
-Well, the question was...
-Mm.

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:06.339
-..."What is your most
embarrassing childhood memory?"

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.407
-Oh, yeah, okay.

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:10.443
I have a couple of times.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:13.813
There was a time I stepped
on ketchup packets deliberately

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:16.315
but covered
our assistant principal.

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:17.416
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:18.717
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:20.953
-We never heard of that.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.754
-Yeah, I made --
I worked hard to make sure

00:05:22.754 --> 00:05:24.557
you never heard about that.
-Your dad -- [ Laughs ]

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:25.758
Your dad's hearing about this
for the first time.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:29.028
-Never heard of that!
But that was not cool.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:32.030
-Poor Ms. Gemila.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:35.000
But, I mean,
I guess the other time was,

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.770
me and my doo-wop group got --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.072
Got stopped by the cops

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:42.474
for singing
Billy Joel in the subway.

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:43.576
[ Ding! ]
-That's it!

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:46.312
That's exactly right!
Come on!

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.080
-Is that really it?
-Yes, that was it!

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.082
That's what he said!
-Yeah.

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:52.285
I'm not embarrassed by that.
-That's what I said.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.554
I said that sounds cool to me.
I would love to --

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:55.821
That sounds like --
Singing doo-wop in the --

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:58.457
-I was embarrassed
that the summons was way more

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:01.560
than we made
while we were panhandling.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.496
-That's where you go
for the echo.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:06.932
-I had to get a lawyer
to help them out.

00:06:06.932 --> 00:06:08.934
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:10.803
It might have been
more embarrassing for you

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.872
than it was for Lin.

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:16.141
-Probably, probably.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.141 --> 00:06:18.611
-We got the score.
You guys are a match.

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.679
You're perfect father and son.
Congratulations.

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:21.814
[ Laughter ]
-Thank you very much.

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.015
-You're welcome.

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.484
Give it up for Luis
and Lin-Manuel Miranda.

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.586
Their documentary
"Siempre, Luis"

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:29.988
premieres tonight on HBO.

00:06:29.988 --> 00:06:32.792
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.694
-I'm sorry about
the ketchup Ms. Gemila.

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:36.729
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.064
-That was funny.

